    "TEACHER FLAG: 0:11:16 «آگے ایک اور مشہور مسئلہ ہے جو کہ احناف اور امام شافعی رحمتہ اللہ علیہ کے درمیان اختلافی ہے» on «ولا قصاص بين الرجل والمرأة فيما دون النفس» → card 4 (ts 0:11:15; quoted in its faida and start_note). No other «اہم / امتحان» remarks in this lesson.",
    "Teacher slips / his own additions (cards follow the book): (a) 0:08:53 «ہڈی کے علاوہ کسی اور دانت میں قصاص نہیں ہے» — reversed; book «ولا قصاص في عظم إلا في السن» = no qisas in any bone except the tooth; card 2 states the book and cites 0:08:52 (reading) + 0:08:59 (his correct reason). (b) 0:07:06–0:07:18 tooth pulled from the root: 'some say uproot, some say file to the root; راجح: uproot' — the matn says «ولو قلع من أصله يقلع الثاني»; the footnote has «وقيل: يبرد إلى موضع أصل السن» and says الكفاية (from المبسوط) holds the tooth is not uprooted but filed; «راجح» is his word — card 2 keeps it as استاد. (c) 0:05:23 'Ali took qisas for sight this way' — book: «مأثور عن جماعة من الصحابة»; footnote الكفاية ٩/١٦٨: in Uthman's time, Ali gave the answer and Uthman judged; Abd al-Razzaq: Ali ordered it. Card gives both. (d) 0:04:28 'today it can be done medically' and 0:04:07 'بدصورتی' as part of the eye reason are his additions (labelled استاد). (e) 0:09:10 'قتل کی تین قسمیں پڑھی تھیں' — the book's كتاب الجنايات opens with five kinds; he names only the three relevant ones; card says '(یہ) قسمیں'. (f) 0:12:19–0:13:06 the nukul (refusal of oath) example (AH: judgment on nukul in limbs, Shafi'i not) is not on pp.30–35; card 4 tamheed labels it as his example. (g) 0:11:39 lists 'کافر مسلمان کو، مسلمان کافر کو' among equal lives — the 02-23 lesson excludes the musta'min; not repeated on the card beyond 'مرد، عورت، غلام، آزاد'. (h) 0:13:26 man's hand 5,000 dirhams, woman's 2,500 — consistent with the bracket note on p.33 («قيمة [يد] الرجل خمس مائة دينار، وقيمة يد المرأة نصفها»; 500 dinars = 5,000 dirhams). (i) 0:26:13–0:26:58 'the qisas-holder cannot take diya without the killer's consent' is his general remark (Hanafi doctrine, not on these pages); card 6 faida labels it. 0:29:13 'killer dies before qisas → nothing' is his analogy (footnote البناية ١٣/١١٥ gives «كالصحيحة إذا تلفت»). (j) 0:34:12 '≈3.5 or 3.75 inches' for 80% — his rough number (80% of a 4-inch head would be 3.2); card keeps only the 80%/20% proportion. 0:35:23 he wavers between 'نو انچ… 10 انچ' and between 'چھوٹا/بڑا' — card follows the book (wound from forehead to nape not reaching the shajj's nape; same option). (k) 0:37:24 attributes 'no qisas even from the root' to Abu Hanifa; the book only says «ولنا» against a riwaya «عن أبي يوسف» (footnote: narrated by Bishr; Qadi Khan) — card 8 says «کتاب «ولنا» کے تحت… (استاد نے اسے امام ابو حنیفہ کا قول کہا)». (l) 0:38:06 Shafi'i's proportional qisas in the dhakar — not in matn/footnotes on p.35; card 8 ikhtilaf labels it «استاد (کتاب اور حاشیے میں نہیں)». (m) 0:27:20 «کسی نے اس کو ظلماً قتل کر دیا، قط ہاتھ کاٹ دیا» — self-corrected to 'cut the hand'; used as corrected. Extension of (k): 0:37:45 «امام ابو یوسف… فرماتے ہیں» — the book has only a riwaya («وعن أبي يوسف», رواه بشر per البناية), not his madhhab; card 8 says «ایک روایت». 0:38:06 «امام ابو یوسف کے ہاں بھی قصاص نہیں» for بعض الذكر is his inference (book states it without attribution); card labels it استاد. 0:04:28 he puts the wet cotton «آنکھ کے اوپر»; book «على وجهه», footnote «ويشد عينه الأخرى» — card follows the book. (o) 0:09:17–0:09:27 he defines shibh 'amd by intention (intent to hit, not to kill); the book defines it by the instrument («شبه العمد يعود إلى الآلة») — card 3 tamheed notes this and lughat gives the book's sense first. (n) 0:25:50 «جس کے وہ انگلیاں کاٹی گئی ہیں» = whose hand was cut (المقطوع); not quoted.",
    "Transcript: 0:08:35 has four lines on one stamp (two ع: and two Urdu) — card 2 cites 0:08:35 for the tooth ruling. 0:05:51 is a ع: line («وفي السن القصاص») and an Urdu line on the same stamp; card 2 ts = 0:05:51. 0:22:02/0:22:03 two ع: lines. 0:30:07–0:30:21 «ولو سقطت المؤوفة» read a third time. No «- خلا:» lines. Header says 86% of lines matched to Whisper.",
